<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Dual-plane auth bootstrap (extend @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy: CIAM + realm discovery; adopt Teams path)</title>
    <phase>P1 Module-host foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:011</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security-sensitive auth code; edits main.tsx auth bootstrap + @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy; tags include auth; token-audience contract risk.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-plane / security-sensitive work with cross-plane token-audience contract judgment — opus per CLAUDE.md §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits main.tsx auth bootstrap (shared frame entry) + @spaarke/auth; auth-sensitive; must not run concurrently with other frame-touching tasks.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>auth, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy for CIAM + per-context authority selection, and wire the shell's
    bootstrap so ONE deployment selects the authority: in Teams → silent Teams SSO (workforce, adopt the
    teams-app-r1 NAA path); in browser → home-realm discovery (explicit "My organization / Partner" chooser)
    → workforce or CIAM authority. Preserve the CIAM sessionStorage per-tab isolation (NFR-05).
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + auth engineer. Follow ADRs strictly. MSAL v5 / Entra CIAM + workforce SSO specialist.</role>

  <goal>
    @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy extended to support a CIAM strategy + config-driven per-context authority; the
    shell bootstrap (main.tsx) selects the plane at load — Teams → createNestablePublicClientApplication workforce
    path (adopt from teams-app-r1); browser → realm chooser → workforce or CIAM. From the SAME URL an external
    (CIAM) and an internal (workforce) user each sign in and reach their launcher. CIAM sign-in keeps sessionStorage
    per-tab isolation.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec FR-03 (dual-plane auth bootstrap) + design.md F2 + ux-brief §3 (Sign-in/realm chooser = explicit
      "My organization / Partner" chooser; Teams = silent SSO, no chooser). The Teams host + MSAL v5 NAA
      (createNestablePublicClientApplication / createTeamsWorkforceMsalInstance) is already proven live by
      teams-app-r1 on external-spa — adopt it, do not rebuild. @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy is workforce-only today
      (Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts:18) — extend for CIAM + plane selection. NFR-05 (documented ADR-028 exception):
      keep the CIAM path on sessionStorage per-tab isolation; the workforce/Teams path may use the standard contract
      where compatible.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/main.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-config.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/host/TeamsHostAdapter.ts</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>011 (shell scaffold). 010 authored the ADR-028 A3 rules this bootstrap obeys (dual-plane, broker-only CIAM, no-OBO workforce).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Preserve the external-SPA sessionStorage per-tab isolation for the CIAM sign-in path (documented ADR-028 exception); do NOT switch the CIAM path to localStorage/@spaarke/auth.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">Broker-only for CIAM (external token authenticates ONLY to the BFF; no OBO); the workforce SPA path is no-OBO and has no Power-Apps-license dependency and no elevation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Adopt the teams-app-r1 Teams host path (createNestablePublicClientApplication NAA) as-is — do not rebuild it; extend @spaarke/auth for the CIAM + realm-selection additions (§11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Follow the Amendment A3 rules authored in task 010 (plane selection by iss/tid on the server; client selects authority by realm/Teams host).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Realm chooser is Fluent v9 (semantic tokens, dark + Teams theme); it never appears inside Teams (silent SSO).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/ux-brief.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/r2-coordination-response.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Teams NAA workforce path" location="src/client/external-spa/src/auth/msal-auth.ts">createNestablePublicClientApplication / createTeamsWorkforceMsalInstance :259 — adopt as-is for the Teams silent-SSO plane.</pattern>
      <pattern name="AuthStrategy extension" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts">AuthStrategy :18 — extend for CIAM + per-context authority.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the teams-app-r1 Teams host + NAA path (main.tsx detectTeamsHost branch, msal-auth.ts createTeamsWorkforceMsalInstance) and the CIAM standalone path (bootstrapStandalone / createStandaloneMsalInstance).</step>
    <step order="2">Extend @spaarke/auth AuthStrategy (Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts) to add a CIAM strategy + config-driven per-context authority selection, without breaking the existing workforce strategy.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement browser home-realm discovery: an explicit Fluent v9 "My organization / Partner" chooser that maps the choice to workforce vs CIAM authority; skip it entirely inside Teams.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire main.tsx bootstrap to select: Teams host → silent Teams SSO (workforce NAA); browser → realm chooser → workforce or CIAM. Keep CIAM on sessionStorage per-tab isolation.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify the CIAM token stays broker-only (no OBO) and the workforce token acquires against api://{workforce-app} (v1) per the teams-app-r1 recipe — confirm audience/authority match before proceeding.</step>
    <step order="6">Build (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; npm run build:prod); verify zero errors.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the token audience/authority contract for either plane does not match the teams-app-r1 recipe (e.g., BFF rejects the acquired token, wrong audience/issuer, or CIAM v2 vs workforce v1 conflict), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do not ship a mismatched auth contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build TS/React (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/main.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/ (CIAM + realm-selection)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same URL in a browser, when an external user picks "Partner", then they authenticate via CIAM and reach their launcher; when an internal user picks "My organization", they authenticate via workforce and reach theirs (FR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the app opened inside Teams, when it loads, then it silently authenticates via Teams SSO (workforce NAA) with no realm chooser shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CIAM sign-in uses sessionStorage per-tab isolation (NFR-05 preserved); the CIAM token is broker-only (no OBO, NFR-01).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an acquired token with a wrong audience/issuer is rejected by the BFF and the escalation trigger fires rather than shipping.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing workforce-only AuthStrategy behavior is not regressed by the CIAM extension.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>@spaarke/auth AuthStrategy (Spaarke.Auth/src/index.ts:18) — workforce-only, single authority. external-spa msal-config.ts already has ciam + workforce-multitenant authority kinds, but no unified per-context selection or realm chooser.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for AuthStrategy (add a CIAM strategy + per-context authority — ADR-010 seam with ≥2 real impls). The realm chooser is a small net-new UI surface required by FR-03; the Teams NAA path is adopted as-is, not rebuilt.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without per-context authority selection + realm discovery, one deployment cannot serve both an external (CIAM) and an internal (workforce) user from the same URL — FR-03 fails and the module-host cannot be single-URL/single-SWA.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Realm chooser (browser)"><steps><step>Load in browser</step><step>Verify "My organization / Partner" chooser renders</step></steps><expected>Fluent v9 chooser; no console errors</expected></test>
    <test name="Teams silent SSO"><steps><step>Load inside Teams host</step></steps><expected>no chooser; silent workforce SSO</expected></test>
    <test name="Dark Mode + Teams theme (ADR-021)"><steps><step>Toggle dark + Teams theme on the chooser</step></steps><expected>zero hardcoded hex; adapts</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    Adopt the teams-app-r1 NAA path (proven live) rather than rebuilding it. Home-realm discovery defaults to an
    explicit chooser (spec Assumption; email-domain sniffing deferred). The BFF already validates both schemes
    (workforce default + CIAM); this task is client-side plane selection only.

    COMPLETION (2026-08-06, FULL rigor / opus): Built via CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path C — did NOT modify @spaarke/auth
    (ADR-028 A3 MUST NOT: module-host SPA MUST NOT route through the Xrm-bound @spaarke/auth). Instead extended the
    sanctioned standalone-MSAL module + main.tsx host branch. New: auth/realm.ts (per-tab sessionStorage realm),
    auth/standalone-plane.ts (realm→{instance,bffScope}; broker-only both planes), components/auth/RealmChooser.tsx
    (ChoiceModal preset, ADR-050/ADR-021). Modified: msal-auth.ts (login-scope seam), AuthGuard.tsx (uses
    getActiveLoginScope; CIAM default unchanged), main.tsx (StandaloneBootstrap state machine; Teams + dev-mock
    branches untouched), App.tsx (clearStoredRealm on sign-out), config.ts (getWorkforceEnvConfig; Teams alias kept).
    CIAM per-tab sessionStorage (msal-config.ts) + Teams NAA path preserved byte-for-byte. Workforce browser plane
    reuses the proven teams-app-r1 workforceAuthorityConfig (same aud/iss) — contract verified by inspection, no
    mismatch, escalation did NOT fire. `npx tsc --noEmit` clean. adr-check + code-review both PASS (0 critical, 0
    blocking). All 5 acceptance criteria met (criterion 4 as invariant; live BFF-reject E2E deferred to P1 tasks
    018/019 — BFF out of scope per NFR-05). Full detail: notes/task-013-deviations.md.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting; follow the task-execute pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
